  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Power Up Anywhere in the World</h2>
  <p>
    So I'm standing in a Lisbon apartment, laptop dying, deadline in two hours. I pull out my charger and... the
    plug doesn't fit. Different shape entirely. Three round holes staring back at me.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is why you need a travel adapter before you need one.
  </p>
  <p>
    Different countries use different outlets—sounds obvious until you're hunting for an electronics store at
    11pm in a city where you don't speak the language. A universal travel adapter fixes this. One device, works
    basically everywhere.
  </p>
  <p>
    I've tested 8 adapters across four continents now. Charged laptops in Tokyo, phones in Dubai, cameras in
    Buenos Aires. Here's what actually matters.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Quick answer:</strong> The <a href="#epicka">Epicka Universal Adapter</a> is my pick for most people.
    Twenty-five bucks, works in 150+ countries, has 5 USB ports, handles your laptop charger no problem. Apple
    person wanting USB-C fast charging? <a href="#satechi-75w">Satechi 75W</a>. That's the short version.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Picks -->
  <h2 id="quick-picks">Top Picks at a Glance</h2>
  <p>In a rush? Epicka for most people, Anker if you need tiny, TESSAN if you're on a budget.</p>
  <ComparisonTable
