  <!-- Understanding Plug Types -->
  <h2 id="plug-types">Understanding Plug Types</h2>
  <p>
    There are like 15+ plug types worldwide. Wild, right? The main ones you'll actually encounter:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Type A/B</strong> is what you know from the US, Canada, Mexico, Japan—flat parallel pins.</li>
    <li><strong>Type C</strong> covers most of Europe, Asia, South America with two round pins.</li>
    <li><strong>Type G</strong> is the UK, Ireland, Singapore thing—three chunky rectangles.</li>
    <li><strong>Type I</strong> shows up in Australia, New Zealand, China with angled flat pins.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A universal adapter covers all these. Every adapter in this guide works in 150-200+ countries. You're covered.
  </p>

